# Organization refactor

- [ ] Remove empty and disconnected artifacts, retire legacy workspace.
- [ ] Correct account, support, telemetry and synchronization ownership.
- [x] Move PDF cache and shared resource-history contract.
- [ ] Split utility responsibilities and remote persistence facade.
- [ ] Distribute command definitions to semantic owners.
- [ ] Split clipper, library, session, capture, DataFn and recovery modules.
- [ ] Resolve semantic naming and audit legacy server retirement.
- [ ] Update architecture enforcement, manifests and ownership documentation.
- [ ] Run architecture, type, unit, compiler and build verification.

Existing test permission: import/mock targets only in the twelve approved files;
PDF-cache test may move. No assertion changes or user-facing behavior changes.

First batch: removed two empty files, the unused Zoho widget, Comment copy,
DragDropTouch and the empty legacy workspace. Account authentication/setup/profile
and Intercom moved to semantic owners. Architecture and type ownership pass;
four PDF-cache tests pass. Account/support ownership complete; telemetry and sync
remain. Cache subtree retirement remains pending.

Additional approval required before splitting the persistence facade:
client/shared-state/files/file-upload.test.ts (import and signed-URL spy target),
client/surfaces/subscription/subscription.test.ts and subscription-failure.test.ts
(module mock target and export shape). Assertions must remain unchanged.

2026-09-22 progress: the three persistence tests were approved and updated.
Facade replaced with semantic runtime transports. Five mixed utility modules
retired and consumers updated. Telemetry and visibility sync moved out of shell;
focus/visibility pulls now share an in-flight request for the same runtime.
Commands distributed to features/surfaces/products with original ordering in a
100-line application assembler. Clipper state split by responsibility. Recovery
split into readers, serialization, identity and conversion; main module 482 lines.
DataFn search/encryption/storage helpers separated. Session snapshot/items/log
construction and notifications extracted. Capture persistence, clipboard,
metadata, completion and location separated. Library query policy extracted.
Renamed TextHighlighter, YearView, CalendarRangePopover; colocated BirdCalendar
with birdView. Removed disconnected cache subtree with one explicitly audited
enum retirement. Legacy server/shared-dbo retained because consumers remain.

Latest tests: 406 passed, two focus-timer tests fail on obsolete private method
spy targets. Need approval for client/features/focus/session-timer.test.ts to
import the notification owner and retarget the two spies, keeping all assertions.
No compatibility methods should be introduced to accommodate old spy targets.
Before completion: formatting, JSDoc/source review, documentation/manifests audit,
full checks/builds and manual verification limitations. Index hash unchanged.
#!/usr/bin/env node

import fs from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";
import { spawnSync } from "node:child_process";
import process from "node:process";
import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";

const SCRIPT_PATH = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);
const SCRIPT_DIR = path.dirname(SCRIPT_PATH);
const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(SCRIPT_DIR, "..", "..");
const NPM_COMMAND = process.platform === "win32" ? "npm.cmd" : "npm";
const DEFAULT_FORMAT = "json";
const SUPPORTED_FORMATS = new Set(["json", "text"]);
const WORKSPACES = [
  {
    name: "@nucleum/app",
    cwd: "apps/nucleus",
    tsconfigPath: "apps/nucleus/tsconfig.json"
  },
  {
    name: "@memotron/app",
    cwd: "apps/memotron",
    tsconfigPath: "apps/memotron/tsconfig.json"
  },
  {
    name: "pointron",
    cwd: "apps/pointron",
    tsconfigPath: "apps/pointron/tsconfig.json"
  },
  {
    name: "timear",
    cwd: "apps/timear",
    tsconfigPath: "apps/timear/tsconfig.json"
  }
];
const ERROR_CODES = {
  baselineFailed: "CHK_BASELINE_FAILED",
  configRollback: "CHK_CONFIG_ROLLBACK",
  reporterUsage: "CHK_REPORTER_USAGE"
};

function sanitizeMessage(message) {
  return String(message).replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim();
}

function stripAnsi(value) {
  return value.replace(/\u001B\[[0-9;]*m/g, "");
}

function toRepoPath(value) {
  return path.relative(REPO_ROOT, value).split(path.sep).join("/");
}

function buildEnvelope({
  status,
  generatedAt,
  workspaceOrder,
  results,
  errors
}) {
  return {
    status,
    generatedAt,
    workspaceOrder,
    results,
    errors
  };
}

function buildUsageFailure(generatedAt, message) {
  return buildEnvelope({
    status: "failed",
    generatedAt,
    workspaceOrder: [],
    results: [],
    errors: [
      {
        code: ERROR_CODES.reporterUsage,
        message
      }
    ]
  });
}

